<!--
    Filter/sliders button, shared by the Home and Explore headers.

    Converted from the Figma header icon (118:445). Path data is verbatim
    from the export, apart from the NaN repair below; the geometry is not redrawn.

    NAN REPAIR: Figma exported 10 malformed "Cnan nan x2 y2 x y" segments —
    cubics whose FIRST control point failed to serialise. They are unexpanded
    smooth curves, so the missing point is the reflection of the previous
    segment's second control point, which is exactly what "S" computes. Both
    export pipelines produced the same defect, so it is the source geometry
    rather than the exporter. Verified two ways before trusting it: this glyph
    and its 16x16 twin (Explore's copy) repair to identical geometry across all
    60 segments after scaling, and a recovered control point mirrors an
    explicit one to 0.001.

    SIZING: the export is a 20x20 leaf; the group maps its 20-unit frame onto
    19.7 units of this 24 viewport — the ink height of ic_notification_bell,
    which is staying and is therefore the fixed reference every other header
    icon is matched to. That also lands within 1.5% of the design's own 20dp
    spec. scale 0.985 with translate (2.15, 2.15) centres it.

    fillType is deliberately absent: the export carries no fill-rule, so it
    uses non-zero, which is Android's default too. Forcing evenOdd would
    invert the knockouts.

    The previous glyph was seven hard rectangles with square knobs; its ink was
    a third lower than the design, so it read much lighter (IoU 0.52, worst of
    the set). This is the designed form: three rounded capsule tracks with
    circular knobs.

    KNOWN DEVIATION: the design renders this at 16dp inside Explore's 40dp
    button but 20dp on Home. One shared drawable cannot do both, so Explore
    renders it at the Home size, ~23% larger than designed. Correcting it needs
    Explore's button padding at 12dp rather than 8dp — deliberately left out of
    the icon pass.

    Tinted per screen by the layouts: wedora_text_secondary on Home,
    wedora_accent on Explore, which is what the design specifies.
-->
